Translation patch: libsignal_protocol (crate attributes)

Change: under the `extraction` feature, `#![feature(register_tool)]` and `#![register_tool(charon)]`.
Why: they make the `#[charon::exclude]` and `#[charon::opaque]` attributes in this crate valid.
Behaviour: unchanged in the production build, which does not enable the `extraction` feature.
Relies on: protocol-Cargo-extraction_feature.patch

diff --git a/rust/protocol/src/lib.rs b/rust/protocol/src/lib.rs
--- a/rust/protocol/src/lib.rs
+++ b/rust/protocol/src/lib.rs
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 
 #![warn(clippy::unwrap_used)]
 #![deny(unsafe_code)]
+#![cfg_attr(feature = "extraction", feature(register_tool))]
+#![cfg_attr(feature = "extraction", register_tool(charon))]
 
